{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490234-what-happens-to-a-wyrd-chimerical-object-once-banality-takes-over","id":1490234,"title":"What happens to a Wyrd chimerical object once Banality takes over?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-15T02:18:23-07:00","id":1490234,"title":"What happens to a Wyrd chimerical object once Banality takes over?","content":"Suppose my Changeling character creates a chimerical object, a vase, that has the Wyrd Rede attached to it so that it is &quot;real.&quot; The vase has other Redes attached to it, like Ensnare, that gives it magical abilities. Eventually, Banality takes over. Obviously, the vase would no longer be magical in any way, but would the vase itself remain in the real world as an ordinary vase, or would the object itself disappear?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26676-squiggles","name":"Squiggles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T07:11:36-07:00","id":1490256,"title":"","content":"If it helps chimerical objects are physical as well, it's just that unenchanted mortals don't notice or remember them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T09:52:40-07:00","id":1490266,"title":"","content":"It is destroyed.<br /> <br /> Solid or not, a Chimerical object is made of dream-stuff. It is not and has never been made of autumn-world material.<br /> <br /> Many Chimerical objects are tied to material objects, but given that's not the case, the vase has no material aspect to it even if it interacts with and is perceived by normal humans. The rede didn't created such aspect. If enough Banality accrues to undo the Chimera (granted, there are no hard rules for when and if that will happen, so it is perfectly plausible to assume that this Chimera can last indefinitely), then the vase vanishes when that happens as it <b>is</b> the undone dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T11:38:10-07:00","id":1490275,"title":"","content":"The vase also would probably be eaten away slowly by Banality in a way that is obvious to the Kithain, unless the Banality that destroys it is very intense.<br /> <br /> Adjectives used to describe that sort of thing are things like worn, tattered, greyed, moth eaten, chipped, etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","user":"zenten","date":". 08-15-2022, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T14:11:45-07:00","id":1490289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490234-what-happens-to-a-wyrd-chimerical-object-once-banality-takes-over?p=1490275#post1490275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vase also would probably be eaten away slowly by Banality in a way that is obvious to the Kithain, unless the Banality that destroys it is very intense.<br /> <br /> Adjectives used to describe that sort of thing are things like worn, tattered, greyed, moth eaten, chipped, etc</div> </div> </div> </div>If its redes make it visible to autumn people, then it is obvious to them too.<br /> <br /> Whatever Banality causes to this Chimera, it will be equally visible to everyone and possibly quite disturbing if it takes hold too quickly or just is a strange mutation. It may also invoke the Mists because of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}